e some measures to  curb the effects of cheating  but truth be told what happened was that  we realized that no matter what we did  it always seemed like the cheating  students would always be one step ahead  of us so on and on we went in this  endless game of two police  now some of you may be laughing at all  of this and perhaps it's a little bit  funny but if you think about it for a  moment don't you think that this  kind of vitiated the entire atmosphere  of learning and evaluation and you know  what were the worst sufferers in this  fiasco is the honest students amongst  you so you suffered in various ways the  direct way in which you suffered was  that while on the one hand you were  studying very honestly for your exams  trying to perform the best in those  exams you could say all around you  students were perhaps less capable than  you and perhaps who had goofed off  enormously and lazily all throughout the  semester they were getting more marks  and higher grades than you there was  another indirect mode of suffering as i  said earlier some of the professors had  taken some measures to curb the cheating  and one of these measures was to set  harder questions so that even though  some of the cheating students  collaborated amongst themselves they  would still find it hard to answer the  individual questions now you can imagine  if  if the questions were set in such a way  that in spite of collaboration they  would find it harder imagine if an  honest student trying to answer this the  these questions on their own without  taking anyone else's help how much  harder will it be from for them  therefore this decision of going back to  offline exams i think it will be most  welcomed not by the professors but by  these honest students  there was actually another kind of  suffering which the honest students had  gone through  so uh initially many of these students  had tried to uh to stay honest and uh  and not take part in any of these unfair  means but as time went by they saw that  they were getting repeatedly beaten by  these dishonest students so ultimately  they just gave up i mean you can only  take so much damage and you can give so  much sacrifice ultimately they also  became dishonest so they went against  their core nature of honesty and  integrity  so that's why i think this kind of an  offline exam will be a much much welcome  respite from all these darker things so  this is about the state of affairs  now let's talk about the consequences of  these offline exams  i believe  and  this is quite obvious that  during this offline exams what is going  to happen is that these students these  cheating students who have become so  much reliant on whatsapp messages and  discord and whatnot there they are going  to finally get caught out their grades  are going to decrease  and basically  it's game over for them and for all  those  false nine pointers out there but what  are the long term consequences of this  so these cheating students their  academic record is going to show up a  peculiar trend before the pandemic hit  their scores would be low  during the time of the online exams this  course would suddenly increase and then  once we go back to the  offline exams their grades would again  decrease  so this kind of a trend in the academic  record it will be a clear and  unmistakable indication that these  students were not just academically less  capable but they were also dishonest all  right their overall grades  may increase we get boost up a little  bit because of what happened during the  online exams uh  the higher grades that they managed to  get through cheating  but this trend of low high low this will  remain forever etched into their  academic record and this is an academic  disgrace that they'll have to carry all  throughout their life now some of you  may be thinking that all right so what i  mean  it's ultimate is the ultimate great  point average that matters but no  i'm quite sure that in the coming years  when it comes for academic kind of  positions and academic interviews when  your transcript is actually looked at by  the professors they will look at this  trend and you will get caught out all  right  some of you  among the  some of the cheating students  they might be thinking that  they somehow managed through unfair  means during the online exams and they  will continue like this during the  offline exams also and uh they will they  manage to get higher grades and here you  are completely wrong okay they'll be  completely wrong on this you see  during the online exams the professors  truth be told were completely  inexperienced okay we did not have  sufficient experience to catch the  cheating and the various unfair means  the students were ahead of us these  teaching students but when it comes to  offline exams there is a wealth of  experience that we can rely on handed  out handed down to us over generations  and generations and don't forget that  all of us have experience as students  ourselves in this offline exams so we  all we know all the inside tricks the  various kinds of unfair means various  permutations and combinations of unfair  means and malpractices the students have  done first  by looking at those kinds of uh of  cheating students when we were students  ourselves and then as faculty members  through our invalidation duty we have  come across so many different kinds of  uh these cases that we know all the  tricks that the students the the  cheating students employ so there is a  distinct possibility that you will be  caught unlike the case of online exams  furthermore there are extremely  stringent and formal measures in place  to handle with such kinds of unfair  means  for example here at iit kharagpur itself  if a student is caught cheating he'll  have to face  a disciplinary committee a formal  disciplinary committee his first his  answer script would be sealing an  envelope and sent to the disciplinary  committee then the student has t